1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,800
A t-shirt order lives in three places.

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:08,800
The brief says 120 shirts.

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:12,800
But the customer emailed: we need 150 now.

4
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:16,800
And the artwork still says 2025.

5
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:19,800
Charge now, and it's wrong.

6
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:25,800
ProofPay reads the brief, the messages and the
artwork together.

7
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:33,900
This run uses a saved AI result for the
sample, so the demo needs no AI key.

8
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:41,800
Five issues block approval. Until they're
settled, the customer can't be asked to pay.

9
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:49,800
Every finding quotes its sources: 120 in the
brief, 150 in the email.

10
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:55,800
For text sources, code checks that each quote
is really there.

11
00:00:56,200 --> 00:01:01,800
On the artwork, it flags the wrong year, date
and website.

12
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:09,800
The merchant settles every finding: confirm
the value, waive it, or dismiss it as an AI
error.

13
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:16,800
For the artwork, the merchant sets what it
must show: the year, the date, the website.

14
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:21,800
Then uploads the corrected file as a new
version.

15
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:29,800
The saved re-check compares field by field:
what was expected, against what was read.

16
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:35,800
Everything is settled, so the order is ready
for the customer at $1,425.

17
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:42,800
The customer sees the exact artwork version,
the amount and the version hash.

18
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:49,800
Approving saves a hash of all of it. Any later
change cancels the approval.

19
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:57,800
Then PayPal, in the sandbox: it authorizes the
payment, but doesn't take the money yet.

20
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:05,800
The money is held until production starts, and
the customer gets a receipt for this version.

21
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:09,800
Paid orders are locked.

22
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:15,800
When production starts, the merchant captures,
and webhooks keep the status in sync.

23
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:20,800
Need a change? Void the hold and reopen the
order.

24
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:25,800
New version, new approval, new payment.

25
00:02:26,200 --> 00:02:32,800
Each payment points at one approved version,
through the custom ID in PayPal's log.

26
00:02:33,100 --> 00:02:42,900
On 3 held-out orders, one run each: 4 of 4 planted issues
found, 0 false blocking findings, 3 of 4 artwork re-check
fields as expected.

27
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:47,800
The model is qwen3-vl, with PayPal Orders,
Payments and webhooks.

28
00:02:48,100 --> 00:02:51,900
AI-assisted verification backed by merchant
and customer confirmation.
